  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe `MessageEvent` object's `origin` attribute seems like it ought to be a serialized origin, and it generally is when it's produced by the browser. When constructed from userland, however, the `origin` string can be pretty much anything, and is reflected back as such (see e.g. https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/webappapis/scripting/events/messageevent-constructor.https.html#L36).\n\nIt would make more sense (to me!) for strings that don't represent valid origins to result in the serialization of an opaque origin (e.g. the above test's `origin: \"testOrigin\"` initialization would result in the `origin` getter returning `null`, not `testOrigin`).\n\nThis isn't terribly important, but it does complicate implementations which choose to hold an origin on `MessageEvent` objects, as might become more common if https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11534 ends up becoming a thing.",
